          Break-even answers an operating question; investor return is a cash-and-exit question.
          Under a capital-gated illustrative stack:
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="ll-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Capital structure</th><th class="num">Amount</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {capitalStructure.map((c) => (
                <tr><td>{c.item}</td><td class="num"><strong>{c.amt}</strong></td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div
          class="pb-chart"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Cumulative operating cash — EBITDA minus about 235 thousand dollars of debt service — by year under the corrected management-target case. Years one and two draw several hundred thousand dollars from opening liquidity. Year three is approximately cash break-even. Later years improve only modestly if the mature transaction band holds. This chart does not show equity payback."
        >
          <div class="pb-plot">
            <div class="pb-line pb-zero" style={`bottom: ${pbPct(0)}%;`}><span>$0</span></div>
            <div class="pb-line pb-equity" style={`bottom: ${pbPct(payback.equity)}%;`}><span>{payback.equityLabel}</span></div>
            <div class="pb-cols">
              {payback.years.map((y) => (
                <div class="pb-col">
                  <div
                    class:list={['pb-bar', { 'pb-neg': y.cum < 0 }]}
                    style={
                      y.cum >= 0
                        ? `bottom: ${pbPct(0)}%; height: ${pbPct(y.cum) - pbPct(0)}%;`
                        : `bottom: ${pbPct(y.cum)}%; height: ${pbPct(0) - pbPct(y.cum)}%;`
                    }
                  >
                    <span class="pb-val">{y.cum < 0 ? `−$${Math.abs(y.cum).toLocaleString()}K` : `$${y.cum.toLocaleString()}K`}</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="pb-year">{y.label}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="figure-note">
          Cumulative operating cash (EBITDA − ≈$235K debt service), pre-tax, under the corrected
          management-target case. Early years draw opening liquidity; Year Three is roughly
          cash break-even at ~85k food transactions. This is a reserve-draw chart, not an equity
          payback claim.
        </p>
        <p>
          The prior “equity paid back in eight seasons” framing is retired. Soft costs alone —
          due diligence/design, POS/technology, pre-opening, and working capital — are more than
          $700K of the current budget and are not dollar-for-dollar recoverable real-estate
          assets. Specialized kitchen, landscaping, and site improvements may also return far
          less than cost on liquidation. <strong>There can be a substantial equity write-off if
          the operating thesis fails</strong>; the downside is not simply a clean property sale.
        </p>
        <p>
          The post-pilot investment memorandum will include what this feasibility plan does not
          yet: a levered IRR, explicit terminal-value assumptions, a replacement-capex reserve,
          and a downside sale scenario. Paths that can still improve investor outcomes after
          pilots clear — continued growth past 85–90k transactions, a refinance after
          stabilization, adaptive-reuse capital well below the $4.6M new-build ceiling, or a
          disciplined exit — remain available, but they are not assumed here. Ownership split,
          distribution policy, and investor preferences are set in that memorandum.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Brand ============ -->
